<Shell title="Plan your Origin89 setup">
<section class="frame page-heading"><span class="micro">Start a site conversation</span><h1>Tell us what<br />runs your site.</h1><p>Start with the equipment you already have and the job you want it to do. Origin89 is in development; this helps us understand your setup and integration needs.</p></section>
<section class="frame page-body form-grid"><form class="plan-form" id="site-plan"><label>What kind of site?<select name="site"><option>Off-grid cottage or remote home</option><option>Maple operation</option><option>Remote field or industrial site</option><option>Another type of site</option></select></label><label>Equipment makes and exact models<textarea name="equipment" id="plan-equipment" placeholder="Solar controller, inverter, batteries, generator, pumps or sensors…" required maxlength="1800"></textarea></label><label>What would you like to monitor or manage?<textarea name="job" placeholder="For example: check battery reserve and inside temperature before the weekend." required maxlength="1800"></textarea></label><label>Internet at the site<select name="connection"><option>Available most of the time</option><option>Intermittent or unreliable</option><option>No internet connection</option><option>Still deciding</option></select></label><button class="action" type="submit">Prepare my email draft <span>↗</span></button><p class="plan-note">Opens an email draft for you to review and send. This preview does not submit or store your details.</p><p id="plan-feedback" class="small-note" role="status"></p><noscript><p class="research-note">To discuss your site, email <a href="mailto:hello@origin89.com">hello@origin89.com</a> with your equipment models and intended use.</p><style>#site-plan>button{display:none}</style></noscript></form><aside class="aside-note"><span class="micro">A useful first conversation</span><h2 style="margin-top:20px">Begin with one<br />job that matters.</h2><p>Which reading do you wish you could check? Which piece of equipment needs a clearer status? Which decision should stay at the site?</p><p>Exact models help us separate existing research, missing interfaces and work that needs hardware testing.</p><a class="text-action" href="/next/equipment/">Browse the equipment catalogue ↗</a></aside></section>
<script>
const form=document.getElementById('site-plan') as HTMLFormElement;
const model=document.getElementById('plan-equipment') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
const selection=new URLSearchParams(location.search);
const selectedModel=selection.get('equipment')??'';
const selectedProfile=selection.get('profile');
model.value=(selectedModel+(selectedModel&&selectedProfile?`\nCatalogue profile: ${selectedProfile}`:'')).slice(0,1800);
form.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();const values=new FormData(form);const body=`Hello Origin89,\n\nI'd like to discuss a setup for my site.\n\nSite: ${values.get('site')}\n\nEquipment:\n${values.get('equipment')}\n\nWhat I want to monitor or manage:\n${values.get('job')}\n\nConnection: ${values.get('connection')}\n`;location.href=`mailto:hello@origin89.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent('My Origin89 site setup')}&body=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;document.getElementById('plan-feedback')!.textContent='Email draft prepared. Review and send it in your email app. If it did not open, write to hello@origin89.com with the details above.';});
</script>
</Shell>
